        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$S$: own state; $I$: interstate; $O$: overseas.\n$S$ only: $18-2x$; $I$ only: $7$; $O$ only: $y$; $S\\cap I$ only: $2x$; $S\\cap O$ only: $2$; $I\\cap O$ only: $x$; all three: $2$; neither: $3$.",
          "worked": "$S$: own state; $I$: interstate; $O$: overseas.\nUse $x$ for overseas and interstate only, and $y$ for overseas only, as defined in part b. Interstate and own state only is $2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Own state only}&=22-2x-2-2\\\\&=18-2x\\end{align*}$$\nPlace each count in its exclusive region.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p19-q24-a-solution-diagram",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 19 p19-q24-a-solution-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,line width=0.8pt,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[black] (-2.5,-2.0) rectangle (2.5,2.3);\n\\draw[black] (0,0.55) circle (1.05);\n\\draw[black] (-0.7,-0.55) circle (1.05);\n\\draw[black] (0.7,-0.55) circle (1.05);\n\\node[anchor=south] at (0,1.75) {$S$};\n\\node[anchor=east] at (-1.9,-0.55) {$I$};\n\\node[anchor=west] at (1.9,-0.55) {$O$};\n\\node at (0,0.85) {$18-2x$};\n\\node at (-0.65,0.13) {$2x$};\n\\node at (0.65,0.13) {$2$};\n\\node at (0,-0.2) {$2$};\n\\node at (-0.95,-0.8) {$7$};\n\\node at (0.95,-0.8) {$y$};\n\\node at (0,-0.95) {$x$};\n\\node at (-2,-1.5) {$3$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
